I have everything needed. Here is the complete extraction of FA3's consumer mainloop schedule for the bf16, head_dim=128, causal case.

---

## Configuration lock-in for bf16 / hd128 / causal

From `tile_size.h:40-45`, `tile_size_fwd_sm90` returns for `element_size==2`, `headdim<=128`, standard (not `use_one_mma_wg`) path:

```cpp
} else if (headdim <= 128) {
    if (use_one_mma_wg) {
        return {64, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 176, true, true};
    } else {
        return {128, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 160, true, true};
    }
```

So `{kBlockM=128, kBlockN=128, MmaPV_is_RS=true, IntraWGOverlap=true}`. These feed the template (`flash_fwd_launch_template.h:45-56`). The derived compile-time switches that gate the schedule (`mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:367-371`):

```cpp
static constexpr bool UseSchedulerBarrier = (IntraWGOverlap
    ? (NumMmaWarpGroups >= 2) && (!Is_FP8 ? kHeadDim <= 128 : kHeadDim >= 128)
    : NumMmaWarpGroups == 2)
    && !LargeHeadDimV;
static constexpr bool RescaleOBeforeGemm = kHeadDim > 128 && (!Is_FP8 || V_colmajor) && IntraWGOverlap;
```

For this case: **`UseSchedulerBarrier = true`**, **`RescaleOBeforeGemm = false`** (128 is not > 128), `MmaPV_is_RS = true`, `HasQv = false`, `Is_FP8 = false`, `LargeHeadDimV = false`. There are **2 MMA warpgroups** (`AtomLayoutQK = Layout<Shape<Int<kBlockM/64>,_1,_1>>` = `<2,1,1>`, line 92), running cooperatively on the same 128-row M-tile (64 rows each). `kStages = 2` (`flash_fwd_launch_template.h:48`). The two MMA warpgroups both call `mma()` (`flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h:437-440`); warpgroup 0 is the TMA producer.

Because `MmaPV_is_RS = true`, every `write_P_to_smem` / `arrive_on_P_write_barrier` block (guarded by `!MmaPV_is_RS`) is **dead code** here, and P (`tOrP`) lives entirely in registers. Because `Is_FP8 = false`, all `permute_*_fp8` calls are dead too.

---

## Q1 — Steady-state consumer inner loop order

The steady state is the `fwd_step` lambda inside the `IntraWGOverlap` branch, `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:1244-1281`. The comment at line 1243 states the pipelining explicitly:

```cpp
// Each step does gemm0 for iter n_block, gemm1 for iter n_block + 1, and softmax for iter n_block.
auto fwd_step = [&](int const n_block, auto mask_fn, auto check_inf_type) {
    static constexpr bool Check_inf = decltype(check_inf_type)::value;
    PipelineState smem_pipe_read_v(smem_pipe_read.index(), smem_pipe_read.phase(), smem_pipe_read.count());
    ++smem_pipe_read;
    Tensor tSrS = partition_fragment_C(tiled_mma_qk, select<0, 1>(TileShape_MNK{}));
    if (!UseSchedulerBarrier || warp_group_idx == 0) { consumer_wait(pipeline_k, smem_pipe_read); }
    warp_scheduler_barrier_sync();                                                                    // (A) acquire tensor-core issue slot
    flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/true, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_qk, tSrQ, tSrK(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read.index()), tSrS);   // (B) QK(i) issue, no wait
    if constexpr (RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }                      // (skipped, hd128)
    if constexpr(!HasQv) {
        if (!UseSchedulerBarrier || warp_group_idx == 0) { consumer_wait(pipeline_v, smem_pipe_read_v); }
    }
    flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, cute::conditional_return<MmaPV_is_RS>(tOrP, tOsP), tOrV(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read_v.index()), tOrO);  // (C) PV(i+1) issue on prev P, no wait
    warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive();                                                                  // (D) hand tensor-core slot to other WG
    warpgroup_wait<1>();                                                                              // (E) wait QK(i) done (PV still in flight)
    pipeline_k.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);  // release K
    if constexpr (HasQv) { ... }                                                                      // (skipped)
    scoremod_premask_fn(tSrS);                                                                        // softcap (skipped, no softcap)
    mask_fn(tSrS, n_block);                                                                            // (F) causal mask on S(i)
    cute::copy(softmax.template max_get_scale</*Is_first=*/false, Check_inf>(tSrS), scores_scale);     // (G) row-max + correction factor
    if constexpr (LargeHeadDimV) { store_scales(scores_scale, smem_pipe_read_v.index()); }             // (skipped)
    softmax.template online_softmax</*Is_first=*/false, Check_inf>(tSrS);                              // (H) exp2 + partial row-sum
    if constexpr (!HasQv) {
        warpgroup_wait<0>();                                                                          // (I) wait PV(i+1) done
        pipeline_v.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read_v);  // release V
    }
    if constexpr (Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor) { flash::permute_Cregs_fp8(tSrS); }                           // (skipped)
    convert_type_out(make_tensor(tSrS.data(), tOrP.layout()), tOrP);                                   // (J) P(i) fp32->bf16 into registers
    if constexpr (Is_FP8 && V_colmajor) { flash::permute_Aregs_fp8(tOrP); }                            // (skipped)
    if constexpr (!MmaPV_is_RS) { write_P_to_smem(tOrP); }                                             // (skipped, RS)
    if constexpr (!RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }                      // (K) O correction AFTER PV
    if constexpr (!MmaPV_is_RS) { arrive_on_P_write_barrier(); }                                       // (skipped, RS)
};
```

So the **exact per-iteration order** for bf16/hd128 is:

1. `++smem_pipe_read`; save `smem_pipe_read_v` = the *previous* index.
2. `consumer_wait(pipeline_k)` — but **only** `warp_group_idx == 0` waits on K (see Q3; WG1 relies on the scheduler barrier instead).
3. **`warp_scheduler_barrier_sync()`** — acquire the tensor-core issue slot.
4. **`gemm(QK)` for block i**, `wg_wait=-1` (issue only: `wgmma.fence` + `wgmma` + `commit_group`, no wait).
5. `consumer_wait(pipeline_v)` for the *previous* block's V (`smem_pipe_read_v`), WG0 only.
6. **`gemm(PV)` for block i+1** (previous block) using the P (`tOrP`) computed last iteration, `wg_wait=-1`.
7. **`warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive()`** — release slot to the other warpgroup.
8. **`warpgroup_wait<1>()`** — QK(i) committed first, so `wait_group 1` guarantees QK is complete while PV is still running.
9. `pipeline_k.consumer_release`.
10. `mask_fn(tSrS)` (causal mask) — runs while PV is still in flight.
11. **`softmax.max_get_scale<Is_first=false>`** → row-max reduction + `scores_scale = exp2(prev_max - cur_max)`, and `row_sum *= scores_scale`.
12. **`softmax.online_softmax<Is_first=false>`** → `scale_apply_exp2` (the SFU `exp2f`) + thread-local row-sum (no cross-thread reduce).
13. **`warpgroup_wait<0>()`** — now wait for PV(i+1) to finish.
14. `pipeline_v.consumer_release`.
15. **`convert_type_out(tSrS → tOrP)`** — P(i) fp32→bf16, kept in registers for the *next* iteration's PV.
16. **`softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale)`** — the O correction, applied **after** the PV gemm (since `RescaleOBeforeGemm==false`).

The three loop drivers that call `fwd_step` are `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:1294-1297` (causal masked region), `1312-1315` (no-mask region), and `1317-1323` (local, skipped for causal). All use `#pragma unroll 1` (no unrolling — see Q5).

---

## Q2 — IntraWGOverlap specifics

**Yes — `gemm(PV)` for block i+1 is issued BEFORE the softmax (max/exp2) of block i+1's *own* scores.** The key insight is the software-pipeline skew: within one `fwd_step`, `gemm(QK)` computes scores for the current `n_block` (via the freshly-incremented `smem_pipe_read.index()`), while `gemm(PV)` consumes `tOrP` — the probabilities produced by the *previous* iteration's softmax — using `smem_pipe_read_v.index()` (the saved previous index). Then the softmax for the current block runs *while PV of the previous block is still executing on the tensor cores*.

The interleave (QK(i) → PV(i+1) → softmax(i)), quoted from lines 1250-1279:

```cpp
warp_scheduler_barrier_sync();
flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/true, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_qk, tSrQ, tSrK(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read.index()), tSrS);   // QK(i)
if constexpr (RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }                                       // NOT taken (hd128)
...
flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, cute::conditional_return<MmaPV_is_RS>(tOrP, tOsP), tOrV(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read_v.index()), tOrO);  // PV(i+1)
warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive();
warpgroup_wait<1>();                          // QK(i) done, PV(i+1) still in flight
pipeline_k.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);
...
mask_fn(tSrS, n_block);
cute::copy(softmax.template max_get_scale</*Is_first=*/false, Check_inf>(tSrS), scores_scale);   // max(i)   } overlap PV(i+1)
softmax.template online_softmax</*Is_first=*/false, Check_inf>(tSrS);                            // exp2(i)  }
warpgroup_wait<0>();                          // now wait PV(i+1)
...
convert_type_out(make_tensor(tSrS.data(), tOrP.layout()), tOrP);   // P(i) -> registers
if constexpr (!RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }   // O-correction AFTER PV
```

**O-correction (rescale) placement:** For hd128, `RescaleOBeforeGemm == false`, so `rescale_o` is applied **AFTER** the PV gemm completes (line 1279), at the tail of the step — it is *not* overlapped with a gemm in this configuration. (Contrast: for hd > 128, `RescaleOBeforeGemm == true` and `rescale_o` is instead placed at line 1252 — right after issuing QK and before issuing PV — so the O-rescale overlaps the QK wgmma. This is the head-dim-dependent difference; hd128 defers it.)

**Prologue (first block, no PV yet)** — `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:1212-1241`:

```cpp
if constexpr (IntraWGOverlap) {
    Tensor tSrS = partition_fragment_C(tiled_mma_qk, select<0, 1>(TileShape_MNK{}));
    consumer_wait(pipeline_k, smem_pipe_read);
    flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/true, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_qk, tSrQ, tSrK(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read.index()), tSrS);
    warpgroup_wait<0>();
    pipeline_k.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);
    ...
    scoremod_premask_fn(tSrS);
    mask.template apply<true /*Seqlenk_mask*/, Is_causal, Is_local>(tSrS, m_block, n_block);
    Tensor scores_scale = softmax.template max_get_scale</*Is_first=*/true, /*Check_inf=*/true>(tSrS);
    softmax.template online_softmax</*Is_first=*/true, /*Check_inf=*/true>(tSrS);
    ...
    Tensor tOrP_acc = make_tensor(tSrS.data(), flash::convert_layout_acc_Aregs<TiledMmaPV>(tSrS.layout()));
    Tensor tOrP = make_tensor_like<Element>(tOrP_acc);
    convert_type_out(tOrP_acc, tOrP);
    ...
    --n_block;
    clear(tOrO);
    auto fwd_step = [&](...) { ... };   // steady state
```

**Epilogue tail (last PV, after the loop)** — `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:1324-1341`:

```cpp
cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(NumMmaThreadsQK + (Use_TMA_Q ? cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp : NumProducerThreads), static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::QueryEmpty));
if constexpr (RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }        // NOT taken
if constexpr (!HasQv) { consumer_wait(pipeline_v, smem_pipe_read); }
flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, cute::conditional_return<MmaPV_is_RS>(tOrP, tOsP), tOrV(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read.index()), tOrO);  // final PV
...
finalize_dispatch(scores_scale, v_descale);       // softmax.finalize(): cross-thread row-sum reduce + inv, LSE
...
warpgroup_wait<0>();
pipeline_v.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);
softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale);             // final O normalization by 1/row_sum
```

So the last block's PV is issued after the loop, and the row-sum normalization is folded into the final `rescale_o` (via `finalize()` returning `1/sum`).

---

## Q3 — Ping-pong vs cooperative

**It is COOPERATIVE tiling (both warpgroups on the same 128-row M-tile, 64 rows each) PLUS a warp-scheduler NamedBarrier that ping-pongs the tensor-core *issue* between the two warpgroups.** There is no `pingpong` template flag anywhere in the hopper directory (grep returned nothing). The mechanism is `UseSchedulerBarrier`, which is `true` here.

The two primitives, `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:952-969`:

```cpp
CUTLASS_DEVICE void
warp_scheduler_barrier_sync() {
    if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
        cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::sync(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) - 1 + flash::canonical_warp_group_idx_nosync() /*id*/);
    }
}

CUTLASS_DEVICE void
warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive() {
    if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
        static_assert(NumMmaWarpGroups == 2 || NumMmaWarpGroups == 3);
        int const cur_WG = flash::canonical_warp_group_idx_nosync() - 1;
        int const next_WG = NumMmaWarpGroups == 2
            ? 1 - cur_WG
            : (cur_WG < NumMmaWarpGroups - 1 ? cur_WG + 1 : 0);
        cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) + next_WG /*id*/);
    }
}
```

`canonical_warp_group_idx_nosync()` = `threadIdx.x / 128` (`utils.h:696-699`); the two MMA warpgroups are indices 1 and 2 (index 0 is the TMA producer, `flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h:320`). So:
- **WG1** waits on barrier id `WarpSchedulerWG1 (=1)`; on arrive, `cur=0, next=1` → signals barrier id `WarpSchedulerWG1 + 1 = WarpSchedulerWG2 (=2)` (WG2's barrier).
- **WG2** waits on barrier id `WarpSchedulerWG1 - 1 + 2 = 2` (WG2's barrier); on arrive, `cur=1, next=0` → signals barrier id `1` (WG1's barrier).

So each warpgroup signals **the other** warpgroup's barrier. `mma_init` (`972-989`) seeds the ping-pong by having only WG1 arrive first:

```cpp
if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
    static_assert(NumMmaWarpGroups == 2 || NumMmaWarpGroups == 3);
    // WG1 needs the very first signal to start
    if (warp_group_idx == 1) {
        cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) /*id*/);
    }
}
```

**What it gates:** In `fwd_step`, `warp_scheduler_barrier_sync()` sits immediately *before* `gemm(QK)` (line 1250→1251), and `warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive()` sits immediately *after* `gemm(PV)` is issued (line 1256→1257). So the barrier brackets the **QK-issue + PV-issue pair**: a warpgroup cannot begin issuing its QK wgmma until the other warpgroup has finished issuing its QK+PV pair and called arrive. This forces the two cooperative warpgroups to alternate their wgmma issue onto the shared tensor pipe (one does QK+PV while the other is in its softmax/exp2 phase), which is exactly the tensor-pipe-utilization trick. Note also the K/V `consumer_wait` is gated by `warp_group_idx == 0` when `UseSchedulerBarrier` is on (lines 1249, 1254) — only WG0... (the lower-indexed consumer) issues the pipeline wait; the scheduler barrier keeps the other WG in lockstep so it doesn't need to re-wait.

In the non-overlap branch (`else`, lines 1345-1429, not used for hd128) the same barrier instead brackets QK-issue via `sync` at 1345/1384 and `arrive` at 1356/1365/1429 — different placement, but for hd128 the `IntraWGOverlap` branch above is the one compiled.

---

## Q4 — The softmax (`softmax.h`)

**Row-max reduction = thread-local reduce then a quad (4-thread) shuffle allreduce.** `reduce_max` (`softmax.h:50-54`) calls `reduce_` (`44-48`) = `thread_reduce_` + `quad_allreduce_`:

```cpp
template<typename Engine0, typename Layout0, typename Engine1, typename Layout1, typename Operator>
__device__ __forceinline__ void quad_allreduce_(Tensor<Engine0, Layout0> &dst, Tensor<Engine1, Layout1> &src, Operator &op) {
    CUTE_STATIC_ASSERT_V(size(dst) == size(src));
    #pragma unroll
    for (int i = 0; i < size(dst); i++) {
        dst(i) = Allreduce<4>::run(src(i), op);
    }
}
```

`Allreduce<4>` (`utils.h:78-98`) is two `__shfl_xor_sync` steps (offset 2 then offset 1) — a **quad shuffle** across the 4 threads that share a row in the wgmma C fragment. No smem, no full-warp reduce.

**`max_get_scale`** (`softmax.h:101-124`) — computes the row max and the online correction factor in one pass, and folds the correction into `row_sum`:

```cpp
template<bool Is_first, bool Check_inf=false, typename Tensor0>
__forceinline__ __device__ TensorT max_get_scale(Tensor0 &acc_s) {
    Tensor scores = make_tensor(acc_s.data(), flash::convert_layout_acc_rowcol(acc_s.layout()));
    static_assert(CUTE_STATIC_V(size<0>(scores)) == kNRows);
    TensorT scores_scale;
    if constexpr (Is_first) {
        flash::template reduce_max</*zero_init=*/true>(scores, row_max);
        cute::fill(scores_scale, 1.f);
    } else {
        Tensor scores_max_prev = make_fragment_like(row_max);
        cute::copy(row_max, scores_max_prev);
        flash::template reduce_max</*zero_init=*/false>(scores, row_max);
        #pragma unroll
        for (int mi = 0; mi < size(row_max); ++mi) {
            float scores_max_cur = !Check_inf
                ? row_max(mi)
                : (row_max(mi) == -INFINITY ? 0.0f : row_max(mi));
            scores_scale(mi) = exp2f((scores_max_prev(mi) - scores_max_cur) * softmax_scale_log2);
            row_sum(mi) *= scores_scale(mi);
        }
    }
    return scores_scale;
};
```

**`online_softmax`** (`softmax.h:126-135`) — applies exp2 and accumulates the row-sum **without** the cross-thread reduce (the reduce is deferred):

```cpp
template<bool Is_first, bool Check_inf=false, typename Tensor0>
__forceinline__ __device__ void online_softmax(Tensor0 &acc_s) {
    Tensor scores = make_tensor(acc_s.data(), flash::convert_layout_acc_rowcol(acc_s.layout()));
    static_assert(CUTE_STATIC_V(size<0>(scores)) == kNRows);
    flash::template scale_apply_exp2</*Scale_max=*/true, Check_inf, Max_offset>(scores, row_max, softmax_scale_log2);
    // We don't do the reduce across threads here since we don't need to use the row_sum.
    // We do that reduce at the end when we need to normalize the softmax.
    flash::reduce_sum</*zero_init=*/Is_first, /*warp_reduce=*/false>(scores, row_sum);
};
```

**The exp2 trick** — `scale_apply_exp2` (`softmax.h:64-88`) fuses the scale and max-subtract into a single FFMA feeding `exp2f`, so the SFU op has no dependent fmul/fadd on its critical path:

```cpp
// Instead of computing exp(x - max), we compute exp2(x * log_2(e) -
// max * log_2(e)). This allows the compiler to use the ffma
// instruction instead of fadd and fmul separately.
tensor(mi, ni) = exp2f(tensor(mi, ni) * scale - max_scaled);
```

`Scale_max=true` precomputes `max_scaled = max(mi)*scale` once per row (line 77-79) outside the `ni` loop, so the inner loop is one FFMA + one `exp2.approx` SFU per element.

**Deferred work (the per-iteration critical-path reduction):** (1) The **row-sum cross-thread reduction is deferred** — `online_softmax` calls `reduce_sum` with `warp_reduce=false` (only thread-local accumulation each iteration). The quad allreduce of `row_sum` happens once in **`finalize`** (`softmax.h:137-154`):

```cpp
__forceinline__ __device__ TensorT finalize(float const final_scale=1.f) {
    SumOp<float> sum_op;
    quad_allreduce_(row_sum, row_sum, sum_op);        // <-- deferred cross-thread row-sum reduce, once
    TensorT scores_scale;
    #pragma unroll
    for (int mi = 0; mi < size(row_sum); ++mi) {
        float sum = row_sum(mi);
        float inv_sum = (sum == 0.f || sum != sum) ? 0.f : 1.f / sum;
        scores_scale(mi) = inv_sum * final_scale;
        ...
        row_sum(mi) = (sum == 0.f || sum != sum) ? -INFINITY : row_max(mi) * (softmax_scale_log2 * float(M_LN2)) + __logf(sum);   // LSE
    }
    return scores_scale;
};
```

(2) The **final O normalization by 1/row_sum is deferred to the epilogue** — during the loop only the per-block *rescale* correction `exp2(prev_max - cur_max)` is applied via `rescale_o`; the `1/sum` divide is folded into the single `finalize()`→`rescale_o` at the loop tail (Q2 tail, line 1339). `rescale_o` itself (`softmax.h:177-187`) is just a per-element fmul:

```cpp
template<typename Tensor1>
__forceinline__ __device__ void rescale_o(Tensor1 &acc_o, TensorT const &scores_scale) {
    Tensor acc_o_rowcol = make_tensor(acc_o.data(), flash::convert_layout_acc_rowcol(acc_o.layout()));
    static_assert(CUTE_STATIC_V(size<0>(acc_o_rowcol)) == kNRows);
    #pragma unroll
    for (int mi = 0; mi < size<0>(acc_o_rowcol); ++mi) {
        #pragma unroll
        for (int ni = 0; ni < size<1>(acc_o_rowcol); ++ni) { acc_o_rowcol(mi, ni) *= scores_scale(mi); }
    }
};
```

For this bf16 config `Max_offset = 0` (`flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h:433`, only FP8 uses 8), so the FP8-specific `sum_scale` and `finalize_aux` branches are inert. `kNRows = 2` for hd128 (`= 2 * (2*kBlockM/NumMmaThreads) = 2*(256/256)`), i.e. each thread owns 2 rows.

**How exp2 overlaps the wgmma:** the overlap is *structural*, not inside `softmax.h`. As shown in Q1/Q2, `max_get_scale` (row-max quad-shuffle) and `online_softmax` (the exp2 SFU sweep) at lines 1268 and 1270 are placed *between* `warpgroup_wait<1>` (line 1258, QK done) and `warpgroup_wait<0>` (line 1272, PV done) — so the SFU exp2 of block i runs while the PV wgmma of block i+1 is still executing on the tensor cores.

